messages:
maria: Heads-up 90m sprint PRs: tightening our function/tool-calling docs + a small migration note for structured outputs. Two PRs: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/450 (examples) and /451 (SDK snippets). Looking for quick reviewers and a short usage blurb for product.

doc-bot: link-checker: PR 450 contains 1 external link warning (cloud-provider docs).

ash: I'll take 450. quick question: do we want `additionalProperties: false` in every sample? my preference is strict schemas for canonical examples, but show a sanctioned `meta` field for extensibility.

sam: +1 to strict canonical schemas. also propose a tiny section "robust parsing patterns" showing an envelope-first parser with graceful fallback to a compact shape and then heuristics. people keep getting partial outputs and it's causing SRE noise.

maria: agreed. draft schema I'm putting into docs/guides/tool-calls.md below (embed as example):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "command": { "type": "string" },
    "payload": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "account_id": { "type": "string" },
        "items": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } }
      },
      "required": ["account_id"],
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "meta": { "type": ["object", "null"] }
  },
  "required": ["command"],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

maria: note: `meta` is explicitly allowed to show how teams can keep a small safe escape hatch. we'll document tradeoffs.

ash: love it. can we add a 1-line product callout: "envelope (structured) = safer routing & typed checks; compact = lower bytes on wire" so readers know why pick one.

sam: adding parser snippets — short and copyable. Python fallback example: 

```py
# envelope -> compact -> heuristic
try:
    result = parse_envelope(resp_text)
except ParseError:
    try:
        result = parse_compact(resp_text)
    except ParseError:
        result = fallback_heuristics(resp_text)
```

# JS equivalent
```js
// envelope -> compact -> simple json
let result;
try {
  result = parseEnvelope(respText);
} catch (e) {
  try {
    result = parseCompact(respText);
  } catch (e2) {
    result = heuristicsFallback(respText);
  }
}
```

maria: nit: across the repo we already have `structured_response` used in a few places. can we standardize on that key? I'll rename instances in the PR.

sam: good catch. also add a short guardrail section: prefer enums for action names, max array sizes, and explicit `additionalProperties: false` unless `meta` is used.

doc-bot: preview-build: docs site preview is live for PR 450 at https://deploy-preview-450--docs.redwood.ai.

maria: action items: ash -> review PR 450 and confirm wording for `meta` use; sam -> add the guardrail paragraph and ensure JS/Py snippets are in sync; I'll normalize `structured_response` and merge once green. Target: Friday noon. :white_check_mark:
